The attributes in this dataset are described in the whv.xls file.
1. Filter out records that have a null value in the TOA [6] or APPT_START_DATE [11] field. Then, randomly select a percentage of the records. The percentage is passed in as a hadoop property. Hadoop properties are set using the -D property=value option.
2. Find the 10 most frequent visitor-visitee combinations.
3. For each visitor (NAMELAST, NAMEFIRST, NAMEMID), find the earliest and latest scheduled appointment dates [11], as well as the total number of scheduled appointments for that visitor.
4. For each hour within a day, determine:
  a. how many appointments were planned [11] ?
  b. how many visitors were delayed?
  c. how much was the average delay time?
  d. how many visitors arrived ahead of time ?
  e. how much was the average speed-up time?
  f. what was the mean absolute error between the scheduled time of the appointment [11] and the time of arrival [6]?

Take into account only those records that contain both dates and the difference between the dates does not exceed 24 hours. Reuse Reducer as a Combiner.

SimpleDateFormat frmtIn = new SimpleDateFormat("MM/dd/yyyy HH:mm");
Date appointmentDate = frmtIn.parse(fields[11]);
SimpleDateFormat frmtOut = new SimpleDateFormat("HH");
int hour = Integer.parseInt(frmtOut.format(appointmentDate));

private long getDateDiff(Date end, Date start) {
  long diffInMillies = end.getTime() - start.getTime();
  TimeUnit tu = TimeUnit.MINUTES;
  return tu.convert(diffInMillies, TimeUnit.MILLISECONDS);
}


